lifeos-nix patch f-inference-provider — local model server, Anthropic as fallback

PROBLEM
  LifeOS can only talk to Anthropic. `claude` is the sole model client, and Inference.ts
  actively deletes ANTHROPIC_BASE_URL. There is no way to run on a local LLM server, and no
  way to keep Anthropic as a safety net — or to forbid it — when one is used.

FIX
  One switch in the USER-zone config, LIFEOS/USER/CONFIG/LIFEOS_CONFIG.toml:

    [inference]
    mode = "local-only"              # anthropic-only | local-with-fallback | local-only
                                     # (default when [inference.local] is set: local-with-fallback)
    [inference.local]
    base_url  = "http://host:port"   # must speak Anthropic /v1/messages
    model     = "name"               # all tiers; [inference.local.models] overrides per tier
    token_env = "VAR"                # optional

  - NEW LIFEOS/TOOLS/InferenceProvider.ts — the decision. Its `gate` subcommand is run by the
    lifeos-nix claude wrapper (pkgs/tools/misc/claude-code/claude-gate.sh) before EVERY exec of
    the real binary; it writes the env delta as shell code plus a sentinel on fd 3, and the
    wrapper execs in place.
  - LifeosConfig.ts: loadRawLifeosConfig() (the TOML without identity validation, uncached) and
    lifeosConfigPath() (so a re-read after a parse error reads the same file).
  - Inference.ts: local-with-fallback retries once on Anthropic when the local attempt fails;
    local-only fails closed. Spawns carry LIFEOS_INFERENCE_TARGET so the gate honours the
    choice; the Anthropic leg is re-scrubbed as upstream intends. Tiers/pinned ids map to local
    model names, and the executed model is verified by that name.

WHAT THE GATE IS (Klemen, 2026-10-07)
  It ROUTES: reads the mode, points claude at the right server, refuses when it cannot decide.
  It does not enumerate what Claude Code can do that reaches Anthropic (subcommands, flags,
  settings sources, providers): that surface changes every release, and five reviews kept
  finding gaps in such lists. The local-only guarantee belongs to the network room (ISA Step
  7c). Kept here because they are static and cheap: strict config keys; a base_url that is not
  an Anthropic host; Bedrock/Vertex/Foundry routing off on the local target; under local-only
  NONESSENTIAL_TRAFFIC on, WebFetch off and claude.ai MCP off.

FAIL-CLOSED
  - Unknown key or bad value in [inference] → refuse. A TOML error refuses unless the file
    cannot be naming inference (no "inference"/"local-only"/"local-with-fallback", no \u escape),
    in which case it is anthropic-only with a warning.
  - local-only never fails over; an Anthropic hint under local-only refuses.
  - The wrapper refuses on any gate error, a missing sentinel (e.g. a stale payload), or an env
    delta that does not apply; the gate runs from / with --config=/dev/null and --no-env-file.
  - No gate found, or LIFEOS_GATE=off: plain claude, unless a config this exec could use may
    name local-only (an unreadable file counts as may) — then refuse.

VERIFIED GOTCHA (why AUTH_TOKEN is always set on the local target)
  With only ANTHROPIC_BASE_URL set, Claude Code sends the subscription OAuth bearer token to
  that URL (measured 2026-10-04). AUTH_TOKEN outranks OAuth, so a server without auth gets
  "lifeos-local-no-auth", never the subscription credential.

KNOWN LIMITS
  Caller-controlled env (HOME, LIFEOS_CONFIG_PATH, CLAUDE_CONFIG_DIR) can steer which config
  and gate are used; an API-key-only user's fallback has no key (the Anthropic leg runs on the
  subscription). Both are the network room's and the next agent's problem, not more gate code.

VERIFICATION
  tests/inference-provider/run.sh — 56 tests against the pinned source + patch list and the
  real gate script with a fake passwd (never the runner's own home): resolution and refusals,
  env overlay/strip, the decide() table, the gate end to end (bunfig preload, stale payload,
  .env, readonly var, health cache, unresolvable uid, no-gate and GATE=off refusals incl.
  escaped and unreadable configs), Inference.ts through the gate. Mutation-checked.

